{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-96837",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{2,3,5,6,7,8,9,10\\},$ and the set $S=\\{2,3,5,6,7,8,9,10\\}$ has $|S|=8$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}, & x=2,3,5,6,7,8,9,10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $3$ items $(8,9,10)$ that satisfy $7<X\\le 10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(7<X\\le 10)=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
